warning[ambiguous_precedence]: operator `|` has lower precedence than `&`
   ┌ test.idl:3:22
   │
 2 │ // Different bitwise operators with confusing precedence
 3 │ const long test1 = 1 | 2 & 3;      // & binds tighter than |
   ·                      ^ ^^^^^ than this expression
   ·                      └─ this operator has lower precedence
 4 │ const long test2 = 1 | 2 ^ 3;      // ^ binds tighter than |
 5 │ const long test3 = 1 ^ 2 & 3;      // & binds tighter than ^
   └──
 help: add parentheses to clarify the intended order of operations

